Read ALL four v7 verdicts, the FULL v8 design and its diff from v7, the oracle README and evidence files, the oracle source/test, and check claims against actual Java and current Go. v8 answers v7: the v7 insert-side inline bound is WITHDRAWN (its key, above the hard cap with neither SPLIT_MERGE nor COLLAPSE, is reachable in the target's own collapse->REASSIGN->reassign flow, and it refused the insert that re-arms the split); the reconcile residue is instead bounded INSIDE the terminal reconcile (typed capacity failure, poisoning, when the reconciled count exceeds primaryClusterHardMax; reachable only where the target's task throws at :397); the inline-delete skip (d) is decided by each task kind's own read-only prologue `consumerOutcome` shared with runTask, including the dependency a head bounce would execute (Java's deterministic pick), with snapshot reads; every typed error raised inside task execution poisons; peel bound ceil(log2 n)+2 with measurements at n=1000 (probe seeds are samples, Go pins its own draws); cost statement corrected (lone cluster evaluates one 1->2 candidate); knob-table measured/source labels corrected; livelock refusal keyed on the knob value (fetch width < 1); reassignNumNeighboringClusters<0 measured; obsolete split under trained bits-9 measured; claim-race fixture split into same-cluster (both complete) and different-cluster (loser typed error) arms; the lease-wait "never lapses" claim qualified to peers with >=10s leases; existing-PK insert exits before the quantizer; declared list (e),(h),(j) restated; forced split/merge obligation limited to Euclidean/cosine with DOT_PRODUCT/EUCLIDEAN_SQUARE pinned failing at the consumer. Challenge sufficiency and interactions with the rest of the design, not only whether the requested words appear. Distinguish measured target facts from remaining source hypotheses.
